  "notes": "GAAP. Governmental = General Fund (only governmental fund); business-type = Water District proprietary fund. Receipts/disbursements from the GAAP fund statements (p6, p8). Business-type net position roll: 4,616,595 + 1,675,731 - 1,308,673 + capital contributions 6,685,160 = 11,668,813. Business-type receipts include interest income and disbursements include interest expense and depreciation; no single totals printed so computed. Balance sheet from government-wide Statement of Net Position, Totals 2025 column (pp1-3). Ending cash = cash + county treasurer + CDs from General Fund balance sheet (restricted cash 13,446 excluded). Detail uses the budgetary-basis budget and actual schedules (pp11-14), which differ from the GAAP statements (e.g. transfers to sinking/expansion funds are printed within revenues and expenditures; treated as other financing, with totals flagged as including them; budgetary General Fund ending balance 1,591,490 differs from GAAP 1,966,857). The operating-expense-by-fund schedule (pp15-16) duplicates these funds on the GAAP basis and was not recorded to avoid double counting. Page 10 (cash flow statement continuation: reconciliation of operating income to net cash, added by the v7 re-trim) adds no new figures. Read pages 1-16 of 16."
